**`app/auth.py`** — `require_api_key` now checks `X-API-Key` header against `VALID_API_KEYS`, raises HTTP 401 (detail: `"Invalid or missing API key"`) when absent or invalid, returns the mapped username on success.

**`app/main.py`** — the changes:

| Endpoint | What changed |
|---|---|
| `GET /tasks` | Added optional `status`, `priority`, `assigned_to` query params (all combinable). Added `page` (default 1) and `page_size` (default 20, max 100) pagination. Filtering runs before slicing. |
| `POST /tasks` | New. Requires auth (`Depends(require_api_key)`). Validates `project_id` exists (404 if not). Auto-generates integer ID (`max(existing) + 1`). Returns 201 + created task. |
| `PUT /tasks/{task_id}` | New. Requires auth. Applies partial updates to `title`, `status`, `priority`, `assigned_to` (only non-`None` fields). Returns 404 if task not found. |
| `DELETE /tasks/{task_id}` | New. Requires auth. Returns 204 on success, 404 if not found. |

All tested: auth rejection (missing key, bad key), bad `project_id`, update/delete on missing task, partial update semantics, combined filtering + pagination.
